bin/
obj/
.vs/
packages/
installer/out/

# Gordan's own working notes — Captain's Log, NBR.docx, the specs he writes for
# me. They were public with the repo for a few hours on 2026-08-23 and he asked
# them out, so docs/ was purged from the whole history. Ignoring it is what stops
# one careless `git add` putting them straight back.
#
# docs/help/ is the EXCEPTION and must stay tracked: it is the source the eleven
# manuals are generated from (tools/make-help.pl), and under the GPL it is the
# manual's source form. Written as docs/* plus an un-ignore rather than a bare
# docs/ so a NEW file under docs/help/ is still seen — a bare rule would ignore
# it silently, which is the failure nobody notices.
docs/*
!docs/help/
